{#
Robots directives
--------------------------------------------------------------
• Preview deploys serve unpublished "ready" drafts (config/draft-utils.js) from a crawlable
  *.pages.dev URL, so the whole environment stays out of search results. Crawling is still
  allowed in robots.txt on purpose — a Disallow'd page can be indexed URL-only, and a blocked
  crawler would never get to read this tag.
• `isIndexable` (src/_data/eleventyComputed.js) decides which pages are noindex for content
  reasons — archived posts and the archive listing. It is shared with src/sitemap.xml.njk so a
  page can never be noindex here yet listed in the sitemap. Those pages stay "follow" so link
  equity keeps flowing to the superseding article (their canonical points at it).
• Order matters: a preview deploy must stay unindexable even when the page is also archived.
• Anything else is left indexable — no tag at all, rather than an explicit "index, follow".
--------------------------------------------------------------
#}
{% if isPreview %}<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
{% elif not isIndexable %}<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{% endif %}
